From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: damnbitimcrit <333091414+damnbitimcrit@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [UI] Paint and present the guest output on a dedicated
 present thread

Xenia's GPU command thread limits the frame rate in Halo 3's busy scenes
(97-99% busy from about 1,600 draws per frame on), and with the presenter
painting immediately, it also painted the guest output and made the host
present call itself: 5-9% of its time in heavy scenes, 30-40% at the frame
cap where the present call blocks.

With host_present_thread (on by default), the refreshing thread only
publishes the image to the guest output mailbox and notifies a dedicated
present thread, which checks the paint mode and paints under
paint_mode_mutex_ like the inline path did, so the UI thread takes painting
over exactly as before. Refreshes during a paint coalesce into one paint
of the newest image, and an image is never presented twice. The thread is
started last in the implementations' initialization and stopped first in
their destructors. GPU loss during its paints goes to the same callback.

The stats keep the GPU thread's time apart from the present thread's: the
GPU thread line shows paints done on it (only with the option off), and a
new "Halo 3 present thread" line shows the present thread's paint time,
allocator waits and host Present, its wakes and their delay after the
refresh, and the guest output images replaced before any paint took them.
